  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "An owner evaluating **branded residences in Europe** should primarily consider the hotel brands that are already most active and credible in the region: **Marriott International brands** such as **Ritz-Carlton**, **St. Regis**, and **W**; **Accor brands** such as **Raffles**, **Fairmont**, **SLS**, and **SO/**; **Four Seasons**; **Kempinski**; **Mandarin Oriental**; **Six Senses**; **Rosewood**; **Hyatt / Park Hyatt / Andaz / Grand Hyatt**; **Hilton / Waldorf Astoria / Conrad**; and **IHG / InterContinental / Regent**.[1][2][4][5][10][15][18]\n\nFor Europe specifically, the market reports also highlight **YOO** as one of the top brands by regional activity, alongside **Kempinski**, **Six Senses**, and **Mandarin Oriental**.[1] At the individual brand level, **Radisson Blu** is described as the most active hotel brand in Europe in one market overview, while **Marriott** remains the overall market leader and **Accor** shows strong pipeline growth.[3][4]\n\nIf the owner is targeting the *ultra-luxury* end of the market, the strongest names to assess are **Four Seasons**, **Mandarin Oriental**, **Rosewood**, and **Aman**.[10][15][18] If the project is more *resort-led* or leisure-oriented, **Six Senses**, **Banyan Tree**, **Kempinski**, and **Falkensteiner** are also relevant, especially in alpine, coastal, and regional resort settings.[2][4][10]\n\nA practical shortlist for Europe would therefore be:\n- **Marriott** family brands: Ritz-Carlton, St. Regis, W, Edition, JW Marriott[5][11][14]\n- **Accor** family brands: Raffles, Fairmont, SLS, SO/, Mövenpick, Rixos[2][9][13][15]\n- **Four Seasons**[5][10][14][15]\n- **Mandarin Oriental**[1][4][10][18]\n- **Six Senses**[1][2][4][10]\n- **Rosewood**[2][5][10][15][18]\n- **Kempinski**[1][2][8]\n- **Hilton** family brands: Waldorf Astoria, Conrad[6][10][15]\n- **Hyatt** family brands: Park Hyatt, Andaz, Grand Hyatt, Hyatt Regency[6][8][10]\n- **IHG** family brands: InterContinental, Regent[6][10]\n- **YOO** and branded-design concepts where the owner wants a non-traditional luxury residential identity[1][2][8]\n\nIf you want, I can turn this into a **developer screening matrix** for Europe, ranking brands by *luxury positioning, regional presence, and suitability for urban vs resort projects*.",
